<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">War Measures Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914–1988</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War Measures Act was a Canadian law of 1914 that gave the federal government emergency powers to rule by decree in times of war, invasion or insurrection. It was used in both world wars, including for the internment of Ukrainian and Japanese Canadians, and in peacetime only once, in the October Crisis of 1970. It was replaced by the Emergencies Act in 1988.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-measures-act.jpg" alt="War Measures Act" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saffron Blaze · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Centre_Block_-_Parliament_Hill.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
